|~ What is declared under `::doc`: the refusals of its constructor
   and the verbs that read a doc's shape for the query. ~|

:doc/construct
  |~~ The doc of a vector of prose strings and quotes. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:doc/PayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::doc` builds a doc from the vector of its segments, prose
      strings and quotes; a payload of another kind is refused.
  ~~|

:doc/PayloadNotVecError/refusesAString
  |~~ A string payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(::doc"x" !| [type /actualType] | eq [::doc/PayloadNotVecError ::string])

:doc/ElementNotSegmentError
  |~~ Every element of a doc is a segment, a string of prose or a
      quote, and another value is refused at the index it stands at.
  ~~|

:doc/ElementNotSegmentError/refusesANumberAmongTheSegments
  |~~ A number among the segments is refused at its index. ~~|
  ::law~(["a" 1] | tag ::doc !| [type /index] | eq [::doc/ElementNotSegmentError 1])

:doc/content
  |~~ The text of the doc: its prose with each quote written where it
      stands.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:doc/content/writesEachQuoteWhereItStands
  |~~ The content writes each quote where it stands in the prose. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~~| | content | eq " a ~(add 1) b ")

:doc/content/readsThePageOfAWord
  |~~ The content of a word's page is its text. ~~|
  ::law~(::vec/join | doc | content | contains "separator")

:doc/content/answer
  |~~ The text of the doc. ~~|
  ::string

:doc/segments
  |~~ The parts of the doc in their order: each run of prose a string
      and each span that reads as code a quote, bare or under the tags
      of its role.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:doc/segments/answer
  |~~ The prose and the quotes of the doc. ~~|
  ::vec

:doc/segments/alternatesProseAndCode
  |~~ Prose and code alternate in the segments. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ a ~(add 1) b ~~| | segments | eq [" a " ~(add 1) " b "])

:doc/segments/keepsTheProseAroundCode
  |~~ The prose on each side of a quote is a segment of its own. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ see ~(add 1) ~~| | segments | count | eq 3)

:doc/links
  |~~ The links of the doc in their order: each quote under a stack of
      tags that holds `::link`, a query a reader follows.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:doc/links/answer
  |~~ The links of the doc, each a query that answers another page. ~~|
  ::vec

:doc/links/findsTheLinkInProse
  |~~ A link inside prose is found. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ see ::link~(::vec | manifest) ~~| | links | count | eq 1)

:doc/links/runsWhereItLeads
  |~~ A link runs the query it holds. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::link~(::vec | manifest) ~~| | links | first | :l / | null | apply l | has ::vec/count)

:doc/snippets
  |~~ The snippets of the doc in their order: each quote under a stack
      of tags that holds `::snippet`, a query a reader runs to see what
      it shows.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:doc/snippets/answer
  |~~ The snippets of the doc, each a query a reader runs. ~~|
  ::vec

:doc/snippets/findsTheSnippetInProse
  |~~ A snippet inside prose is found. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ run ::snippet~([2 1] | sort) ~~| | snippets | count | eq 1)

:doc/snippets/opensToWhatItShows
  |~~ A snippet opens to what it shows. ~~|
  ::law~(|~~ ::snippet~([2 1] | sort) ~~| | snippets * open | eq [[1 2]])
